  "keyboard": [
    {
      "keys": ["Tab", "Shift+Tab"],
      "effect": "Moves the focus to the trigger and on to the next or the previous control. A disabled select menu is skipped."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["Enter", "Space", "ArrowDown", "ArrowUp"],
      "effect": "Opens the list with the focus in its search."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["A letter"],
      "effect": "In the search, narrows the options to those that match what is typed."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["ArrowDown", "ArrowUp"],
      "effect": "Moves to the next or the previous option, past the disabled ones, with the focus kept in the search."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["Home", "End"],
      "effect": "Moves to the first or the last option."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["Enter"],
      "effect": "Chooses the option. With one choice it closes the list and puts the focus back on the trigger; with several it adds or takes away the option and keeps the list open."
    },
    {
      "keys": ["Escape"],
      "effect": "Closes the list, and puts the focus back on the trigger."
    }
  ],
  "aria": {
    "pattern": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/combobox/",
    "rules": [
      "The trigger is a combobox: `aria-expanded` says whether the list is open, and `aria-controls` names the list.",
      "The label is a label element for the trigger: its accessible name. The help and the error are its description, by `aria-describedby`, and a select menu in error has `aria-invalid` true.",
      "The search is a text field with an accessible name, such as Search cities, and `aria-activedescendant` names the option the arrow keys are on, so the focus stays in it.",
      "The list is a listbox, its options are options, and each chosen one has `aria-selected` true. With several choices the listbox has `aria-multiselectable` true.",
      "When the search matches nothing, the list says so in words, which assistive technology reads.",
      "The chevron, the tick, the search icon and the loading icon are hidden from assistive technology."
    ]
  },
  "forcedColors": [
    "The edge of the trigger is a real border, which forced colors keep in the system's colors, and in `GrayText` when the select is disabled.",
    "The list's edge is a real border too, so the list stands apart from the page under it, which forced colors paint in the same color as the list.",
    "The option the pointer or the arrow keys are on is outlined in `Highlight`, as its fill is gone.",
    "The focus ring is an outline, which forced colors keep. The icons take the system's text color."
  ],
  "motion": [
    "The edge changes color in `motion.duration.fast`, with `motion.easing.standard`. With `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` it changes at once.",
    "The list fades in and grows a little from the trigger in `motion.duration.fast`, with `motion.easing.out`, and goes as it came, with `motion.easing.in`. With less motion it only fades.",
    "The loading icon turns only with `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`."
  ],
  "content": [
    "The label names what is chosen, in sentence case and with no colon: City, Day.",
    "No placeholder. What to choose, or why, goes in the help under the field: Where the conference takes place.",
    "An option is a value, as the reader would say it: Day one, May 10. A group's name says what its options share: Workshops.",
    "The search's placeholder says what it searches, as the field above it names it: Search cities. It is the one placeholder the system draws, as the search has no label of its own.",
    "With no match, the list says so plainly: No city found.",
    "An error says how to fix it: Choose the day you are registering for."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The form field around a select, its label, required mark, help and error, is the input spec's, at the same sizes: this spec holds the trigger and its list.",
    "The trigger's chevron is always drawn, so the choice ends past it: the padding at the end is the field's padding, the icon and the control's gap. An icon sits inside the edge, where the choice starts.",
    "An option's leading icon and its description, under its label in the secondary text, are drawn as an implementation draws them and not checked yet. A disabled option is `color.text-faint`, exempt from contrast as WCAG exempts an inactive control.",
    "The search is a field without an edge of its own, at the control's height of the select menu's size, its icon at the control's icon size, on the panel's edge, with a line of `color.border` under it.",
    "With several choices, the trigger shows them as the implementation lays them out. This spec holds the one look of a choice.",
    "A gallery draws the open list in place, under its trigger and inside the example, not in a layer at the end of the page, so that a test finds it by the example's id. Its first option is the chosen one, which the list opens on and highlights. The element with the example's id wraps the select itself, its trigger and its list, and never its form field or a field nested in it: the form field's label is a slot of its own, which an implementation's list may use for a group's name."
  ],
  "implementations": {
    "ui-vue": {
      "library": "Nuxt UI 4.12, themed by ui-vue's app config",
      "status": "shipped",
      "parity": "none",
      "components": ["USelectMenu", "UFormField"],
      "today": "The outline variant in Nuxt UI's five sizes, inside a form field, as ui-vue's select draws it, with a search field at the top of the list on a line of `color.border`, the bare input of ui-vue, at the control's height.",
      "parts": {
        "root": "base",
        "placeholder": "base placeholder",
        "leading-icon": "base leadingIcon",
        "trailing-icon": "base trailingIcon",
        "content": "content",
        "group": "group",
        "group-label": "content label",
        "item": "item",
        "item-highlight": "item::before",
        "item-indicator": "itemTrailingIcon",
        "separator": "separator",
        "search": "input",
        "search-icon": "input leadingIcon"
      },
      "variants": {
        "outline": {
          "variant": "outline"
        }
      },
      "sizes": {
        "xs": {
          "size": "xs"
        },
        "sm": {
          "size": "sm"
        },
        "md": {
          "size": "md"
        },
        "lg": {
          "size": "lg"
        },
        "xl": {
          "size": "xl"
        }
      },
      "deviations": [
        {
          "summary": "The list's edge is an inset ring, a box shadow, and a border only in forced colors. So the rows for the content's `border-color`, `border-style` and `border-width` do not hold, nor its `box-shadow` of none."
        },
        {
          "summary": "The list's edge is `color.border`, 1.57:1 on the list in the dark theme and 1.33:1 in the light one, where the spec takes `overlay.border`, the field border, which reads at 3:1."
        },
        {
          "summary": "The list reads the roles by their Tailwind utilities, such as `bg-surface`, and a size's paddings and icons by Tailwind's spacing, such as `size-5`, not the component tokens, such as `bg-(--ws-overlay-bg)`, so a change of the tier does not reach it."
        },
        {
          "summary": "Its gallery marks no example with `data-spec`, and draws no list open: a list opens in a layer at the end of the page, outside its example."
        }
      ],
      "beyond": [
        "The variants soft, subtle, ghost and none.",
        "An option's avatar and chip, creating an option from the search, and the trigger's own search field, with the `searchInput` in the trigger."
      ]
    },
    "ui-react": {
      "library": "shadcn/ui on Radix",
      "status": "planned",
      "parity": "none"
    }
  },
